<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="032" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Extracted invoices carry Matter field mapping: an allow-listed, gated, fill-only mapping step inside InvoiceSubmissionPersister, before its transaction (FR-20; owner ruling 2026-11-06; reviews 2026-11-07)</title>
    <phase>3 W3 Product creators onto the service</phase>
    <gate>Round-3 confirmations, recorded in notes/decisions.md, for each item of notes/task-032-design.md section 14:
      (1) the owner approves moving Repair's gate and fit logic into MappingWriteGates;
      (2) ebilling-r1 AND UAC-r2 sign off the allow-list;
      (3) the owner chooses option A, B or C for FR-20's value;
      (4) ebilling-r1 confirms the one-parameter constructor;
      (5) UAC-r2 confirms ReadCoverageAsync for the No Access read;
      (6) UAC-r2 confirms "no admin note" for a Secure core.
    No code before then.</gate>
    <status>blocked</status>
    <blocked-reason>Round-3 confirmations (design section 14). Base branch: section 15.</blocked-reason>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api, including a RecordCreationService partial (a move, with the owner's approval). Tags include bff-api, finance and security. The step writes into a one-transaction create with fixed ids as the system principal. It changes guarded ArchTests (#2188 mask guard, FeatureRolePrivilegeGuardTests) and adds tests at KEEP paths.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The design fixes the placement, the principal, the allow-list, the deny-list, the gate, the fault rules, the re-commit and the guards, so each part is executed literally. Escalate to opus if a round-3 answer changes the design.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W3-server</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits ebilling-r1's InvoiceSubmissionPersister.cs, AdminAttentionText.cs and FinanceModule.cs, and fm's RecordCreationService.Repair.cs. Sequence after eb 165d and 095d-2b-3 and run /conflict-check.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>019; 052a (merged: IGenericEntityService.GetColumnMetadataAsync); round-3 gate; the base branch of design section 15</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, finance, security, field-mapping, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>22-29 hours, executed as three PRs: 032a (5-7 h), 032b (9-12 h), 032c (8-10 h)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement notes/task-032-design.md (round 2) exactly, in three parts.

- **032a** moves Repair's secure-source and target-fit logic, unchanged, into `Services/RecordCreation/MappingWriteGates.cs`. Repair delegates to it. 032a also adds the role-source assertion G5.
- **032b** adds the scoped class `InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping`. Its outcomes: owner gate, profile, then the allow-list (primary) and deny-list (second check), No Access, metadata per delivery, source read as `MappingSourceReader.System`, the secure-source gate, `ApplyFillOnly` all-or-nothing, fit, and copy.
- **032c** wires the class into `PersistCoreAsync`:
  - one optional constructor parameter;
  - the call between the review-detail write and `BuildInvoiceCreateRequest`;
  - `OwnedInvoiceColumns`;
  - the local-function commit with one mapping-free re-commit;
  - the `AdminAttentionText` mapping segment;
  - the FinanceModule registration.

Fill-only: an extracted or persister value always wins. Never call `RecordCreationService` itself. A fault never fails, refuses or retries the submission.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, e-billing submission persistence and field mapping. Follow ADRs strictly. The design is the contract: where it and this POML disagree, stop and ask.</role>
  <goal>A submission whose core record (matter, project or work assignment) has an active field-mapping profile to sprk_invoice, with rules into allow-listed columns, produces an invoice whose unsupplied allow-listed columns are filled from that core record. This happens in the same single transaction and with the same deterministic ids, unless the gate, a fault or a fit check says otherwise, in which case nothing is mapped. Every other submission persists exactly as today.</goal>

  <context>
