  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner ruling 2026-11-06">Creator: InvoiceSubmissionPersister stays the only code that creates the invoice family on the extraction path. No new creator, no second transaction, and no call to any RecordCreationService instance member.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner ruling 2026-11-06; design 5.3">RecordCreationService: nothing is added to it. The ONLY permitted diff is 032a's move of SourceMayBeCopiedAsync, SourceGateColumns and TargetColumnValue (with IsNumberType, AsNumber and InRange) into MappingWriteGates, with the Repair methods as wrappers that keep their log lines and behaviour. It needs the owner's approval first (gate item 1). The Repair suites pass with no assertion changed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-02">Precedence: fill-only through CreateTimeFieldMapping.ApplyFillOnly, unchanged (no new parameter), on a copy of the invoice as the persister built it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C1; Q-U6; design 6.1">Allow-list (primary): a rule is applied only when its target is in InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping.AllowedTargets, the set signed off in round 3 (proposed: sprk_description, sprk_highpriority). Every entry is of a type ColumnMetadata fully checks: no Decimal, Double, Money or DateTime column.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C1; Q-U2; Q-E3; Q-E5; C5; design 6.2">Deny-list (second check): every group of design 6.2 refuses its targets even when allow-listed. The groups are read by reference: ProtectedFromMapping, RefuseAppOnlyWrite, the status pair and the id, InvoiceSubmissionPersister.OwnedInvoiceColumns (including the five Q-E3 columns), InvoiceIndexDocument.InvoiceColumns and the search-index columns, the runtime ExternalModuleRegistry ReadableColumns for sprk_invoice, the access-conferring columns (canonical and bound), contact, systemuser and team lookups, filing lookups (both IsFilingLookup overloads), sprk_billingexport and sprk_invoiceduedate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C2; Q-U5; UAC-r2 follow-up; EB-D-207; design 5">Gate: map nothing when owner.IsSecureOwner, when owner.InPlaceOfDefaultTeamId is set (hard-deny), when an active, well-formed No Access entry covers the core record (ReadCoverageAsync, then ReadEntryAsync, then TryClassify; truncated counts as covered), or when MappingSourceCopyGate says Secure. Gated outcomes log a code and write NO admin note. A failed read (coverage, entry, secure team) maps nothing and writes the note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028; design 4">Identity: the profile, metadata, No Access and source are read app-only as the system principal (MappingSourceReader.System). No OBO, no impersonation and no caller probe. The source is only outcome.CoreRecord, passed explicitly. MappingSourceResolver is never called.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Q-U4; design 7">Field security and metadata: GetColumnMetadataAsync is called for the core table and sprk_invoice on every delivery that reaches it, with no cache. A fault, an empty answer, or an unknown IsSecured on a needed source column maps nothing (note). A source column missing from a successful answer drops only its rule, with a Warning naming the rule id. A secured source column is never read. A target that is not IsSecured == false is dropped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C3; design 8.2">All or nothing: any warning ApplyFillOnly adds, or any written column that fails MappedTargetFit, maps nothing and writes the note (rule_fault or value_unfit). No partial set ever reaches the invoice.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C4; design 3.3">Determinism: the protected resolver keys are the static CreateTimeFieldMapping.RegardingPairAndResolverColumns. Rules are sorted by (ExecutionOrder, Id) before the engine runs. Lookups are checked with the MappedLookup overload of IsFilingLookup.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Q-E1; design 9">Transaction: ids, request order and count are unchanged. The commit and its full catch chain are one local function, called at most twice. A second call happens only when FailedRequestIndex == 0, the step applied at least one column, and the outcome is known. Before it, create.Requests and the submission update are rebuilt at the same indexes with the mapped columns removed and the note create_refused_with_mapping. If the count or an index would differ, return the ordinary Retry. ResumeAsync never maps.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Q-E2; design 8.3">Admin note: one AdminAttentionText segment kind ("Field mapping not applied: " plus one code), for faults only, in the fixed order signals, policy, mapping, stopped, undone. Merge and WithoutStopped recognise it. The Signal segment shrinks so the whole text stays within AdminAttentionMaxLength (500) and the mapping segment is never cut.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Q-E6; ADR-010; CLAUDE.md §11">DI: one new registration, AddScoped&lt;InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping&gt;() in FinanceModule (concrete, no interface, so the ADR010_DITests ceiling is unchanged). The persister gains one optional trailing parameter. When it is null, the step does not run and one Warning not_wired is logged per persist. If ebilling-r1 picks the five-parameter fallback in round 3, follow design 3.1 instead.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C5">Money guard: InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping names no money or firm column, and reaches them only through OwnedInvoiceColumns and ProtectedFromMapping. InvoiceMoneyColumnsAppOnlyWriteGuardTests passes unchanged unless ebilling-r1 lists the step under Readers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Logs and the note carry codes, column names, rule ids and record ids only, never a mapped or extracted value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF publish: Placement Justification in each PR, the fresh-master publish-size delta, `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`, and no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038; testing.md:132">Tests: new tests go under tests/unit/domain/** and tests/Spaarke.ArchTests only. Existing tests change only to follow a moved dependency, never by weakening an assertion. Every guard ships with must-fire and must-not-fire controls, and every behaviour test is shown red first.</constraint>
  </constraints>

