  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor. Confirm the round-3 answers in decisions.md. Cut the part's branch from the base in design section 15 and run /conflict-check. Re-grep every line the design cites.</step>
    <step order="1" name="032a">Write T-M1 and G5 red. Move the Repair logic into MappingWriteGates unchanged and make Repair delegate. Run the Repair suites unchanged, FeatureRolePrivilegeGuardTests and T-M1. One adversarial pass.</step>
    <step order="2" name="032b">Write the step's tests red (T-P2-4, T-G1, T-S1-2, T-C3-4, T-V1, T-F1-2, G3). Add InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping following design sections 3 and 5-8, and the #2188 entry. Two adversarial passes (security).</step>
    <step order="3" name="032c">Write the persister tests red (T-P1, T-T1-2, T-I1, T-R1, T-E4, T-A1, T-DI, G1). Add OwnedInvoiceColumns, the parameter, the call, the local-function commit and re-commit, the AdminAttentionText segment and the registration. Run the regression list of design section 11. One adversarial pass.</step>
    <step order="4">For each part: build, publish-size delta, CVE check, notes in notes/task-032-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A round-3 answer changes the placement, the principal, the allow-list, the gate or the fault rule: STOP. The design is re-issued before code.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any RecordCreationService*.cs change beyond 032a's approved move and wrappers: STOP.</trigger>
    <trigger>A Repair test must change to pass after the move: STOP. The move was not behaviour-preserving.</trigger>
    <trigger>The persister on the base branch has no single point after the last persister-written invoice column and before BuildInvoiceCreateRequest, or create.Requests is not rebuildable at the same indexes: STOP and ask ebilling-r1.</trigger>
    <trigger>An allow-listed column turns out to be partner-readable, indexed, access-conferring or persister-written: STOP. The allow-list is reviewed again.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>RecordCreationService.MapFieldsAsync (caller principal) and RepairMappingAsync (system principal) are the engine's two callers. Both are private, and the ruling keeps the service closed. Repair's SourceMayBeCopiedAsync and TargetColumnValue are private too.</existing>
    <extension>The engine (CreateTimeFieldMapping, MappingSourceReadProbe, the service's internal static helpers) is reused unchanged. Repair's gate and fit logic is moved, not copied, so the step and Repair share one implementation (UAC-r2 "reuse, not a re-implementation"). The step class holds only the invoice-specific allow-list, deny-list, gate order and fault rules.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-20 is not met for extracted invoices: no invoice from the submission job gets core-record fields, which the owner ruling of 2026-11-06 requires in R1. The scoped registration (rather than parameters) is the cost of the gate UAC-r2 required: six dependencies that the persister would otherwise take one by one.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

