  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AC1 Placement (032c): PersistCoreAsync calls ApplyAsync exactly once per non-resume persist, after FillInvoice, the creator stamp, sprk_submittedby, the supersedes link and the review detail, and before BuildInvoiceCreateRequest. The invoice create carries the mapped columns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC2 Allow-list (032b): a Copy into sprk_description or sprk_highpriority fills it, for a matter, a project and a work-assignment core record. A rule into any other column, including the dev profile's four attorney and paralegal targets, writes nothing. G3 pins the exact set, its disjointness from every design 6.2 group, its types and its ValidForCreateApi, with must-fire seeds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC3 Deny-list (032b, negative): one test per design 6.2 group and per Q-E3 column. An allow-listed copy of the column is still refused, including when the persister left the column empty.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC4 Fill-only (032b/032c): a persister-set value is never overwritten.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC5 Gate (032b, T-G1): a Secure owner, a hard-deny owner, a covering active and well-formed No Access entry (record, organization wall, Secure parent), truncated coverage, and a Secure or flagged source each map nothing with NO note and a log code. The owner cases make no read. Unreadable coverage, an entry read fault and an unresolved Secure team map nothing WITH the note. An inactive or malformed entry, and an ordinary core record, map.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC6 Field security and metadata (032b): a secured source column is never read or mapped. A metadata fault, an empty answer or an unknown IsSecured maps nothing with the note. A missing source column drops only its rule, with a Warning naming the rule id. Metadata is read twice per delivery and again on the next delivery (no cache).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC7 All or nothing (032b): any engine warning maps nothing (note rule_fault). Any written column failing MappedTargetFit (type, length, range, lookup table, option) maps nothing (note value_unfit).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC8 Determinism (032b): shuffled rules with equal ExecutionOrder give the same result. A filing lookup is refused through the MappedLookup overload.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC9 Faults never fail the submission (032b/032c): every fault gives the same status, reason code, ids, request order and count as no profile. No profile, an empty profile, or every rule skipped writes no note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC10 Re-commit (032c, T-R1): refused once at index 0 with mapping, the second execution commits without the mapped columns, with the note. Refused twice: Retry, two executions. Nothing mapped: Retry, one execution. Another index: the existing chain, one execution. Outcome unknown: no re-commit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC11 Re-delivery (032c, T-E4, T-T2): two deliveries, the first rolled back, store exactly the second's values and note. A resumed submission makes no profile, metadata, No Access or source read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC12 Admin note (032c, T-A1): the cap test holds (at most 500 characters, mapping segment whole, Signal segment truncated with "(+N more)"), the order is fixed, and WithoutStopped keeps the mapping segment.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC13 DI (032c, T-DI): from the real container, the persister resolves with a non-null InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping whose dependencies are all non-null. With it null, one Warning not_wired is logged and nothing is mapped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC14 Identity (032b): the source read names outcome.CoreRecord with MappingSourceReader.System. No OBO client or probe is used.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC15 Guards: G1 (call position, single caller, no ResumeAsync call, invoice local only, allowed RecordCreationService statics only, System reader literal, gate before engine) with controls. G2: the #2188 guard passes with one entry, Uses = 1, and KnownCallSites = 4. G4: InvoiceMoneyColumnsAppOnlyWriteGuardTests passes. G5 (032a): role-source assertion with a must-fire seeded role and must-not-fire real files. G6: the census passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC16 Move (032a): the Repair suites (RecordRepairColumnMetadataTests, RecordRepairColumnValueTests and the Repair mapping tests) pass with no assertion changed. T-M1 covers MappingWriteGates directly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC17 Unchanged: no change to CreateTimeFieldMapping, RecordTableRules, ColumnMetadata, InvoiceSubmissionRerunJobHandler or the handler. The only RecordCreationService*.cs diff is 032a's move. ADR010_DITests is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC18 Each part: the BFF builds with 0 errors; the publish-size delta and CVE result are recorded in notes/task-032-notes.md.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

